{
  "name": "Start",
  "comment": "A call in parallel answers a task, and the next step runs before the called goal ends: Slow sleeps, then reads\n%order% — its reads fall through to the caller's memory, live — so it reads what the step after the call wrote.\nWhat the task writes stays in it: the caller's %order% is its own.",
